course: dictionary
lesson: 14454
title: Parasitic: living off others
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Parasitic describes something that lives on or inside another living thing, called the host, and takes food from it. Often the host is harmed. «The tick is a parasitic animal that lives on a dog and feeds on its blood.» The dog is the host, and the tick is the parasite that takes from it.
explain: Parasitic can also describe a disease caused by parasites. «The doctor said the child had a parasitic worm, so she must wash her hands often.» Here parasitic tells you the illness comes from tiny living things that feed on the body.
explain: Sometimes parasitic is used about people, and it is not kind. «Greedy Sam is parasitic: he takes everyone's sweets and never shares.» Sam is taking from others and giving nothing back, so the word shows disapproval. Look at the clues around the word to find out which meaning is being used.
fact: Parasitic means living on or inside another living thing and taking food from it.
fact: The living thing that the parasite lives on is called the host.
fact: «Parasitic» can also mean caused by parasites, as in «a parasitic disease».
fact: Fleas, ticks, head lice, tapeworms and mistletoe are all parasitic.
fact: About people, «parasitic» means taking from others without giving anything back.
exercise: «Fleas are parasitic and live on a cat.» In this sentence, what is the host? | The garden | The vet | The flea | *The cat
exercise: «The tick is a parasitic animal that lives on a dog.» What does parasitic mean here? | Living only in the sea | Able to fly very fast | Kind to other animals | *Living on another living thing and taking food from it
exercise: «Greedy Sam is parasitic: he takes everyone's sweets and never shares.» What does parasitic suggest about Sam? | He is a clever inventor | *He takes from others and gives nothing back | He is a small insect | He is very kind and shares everything
test: Which of these is a parasitic plant? | Rose bush | Grass | Oak tree | *Mistletoe
test: Why does washing your hands help against parasitic worms? | It makes the worms grow bigger | It gives the worms food | *It stops the worms spreading to you | It makes the worms fly away
exam: Which person is described as parasitic? | *A child who takes others' snacks and never shares, and never gives anything back | A child who always takes others' snacks and never shares | A child who helps wash up after dinner | A child who shares her crisps with friends
